# Every text file is LF in every checkout, whatever the machine's core.autocrlf.
# Git for Windows defaults to autocrlf=true, and the Windows runner (phase 7a)
# would then check out CRLF: the content check hashes the TOML's bytes and
# calls the artifact stale, and bash refuses the deploy scripts.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The palette exactly as downloaded. Its mixed line endings are part of the
# canonical source the swatches regenerate from byte for byte.
packages/asset-contract/palettes/resurrect64.hex -text

# The translation review sheets exactly as exported: CRLF rows and a UTF-8 BOM,
# which spreadsheet apps need to open CJK text correctly (docs/i18n/README.md).
docs/i18n/review/*.csv -text
